@startuml DCD_UC2_RecordDecision
title Design Class Diagram - UC2 Record a Proposal Decision

top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 75

class ProposalController <<controller>> {
  +recordDecision(proposal, outcome, conditions, note)
}

class ProposalRepository <<repository>> {
  +find(proposal): Proposal
  +save(proposal)
}

interface Clock {
  +currentDate(): Date
}

class Proposal {
  subject
  intendedAudience
  format
  expectedDuration
  preferredPublicationPeriod
  programmeType
  proposedBy
  --
  +canRecordDecision(): boolean
  +recordDecision(outcome, editor, today, conditions, note)
  +currentState()
}

class ProposalDecision {
  outcome: DecisionOutcome
  decisionDate: Date
  conditions
  note
  decidedBy
  --
  +leavesProposalOpen(): boolean
}

enum DecisionOutcome {
  accepted
  rejected
  returnedForRevision
  heldForFutureConsideration
}

ProposalController ..> Proposal : delegates
ProposalController ..> ProposalRepository : uses
ProposalController ..> Clock : uses
ProposalRepository ..> Proposal : stores
Proposal "1" -- "0..*" ProposalDecision : receives
ProposalDecision ..> DecisionOutcome : outcome

note right of Proposal
  Current state is derived from the latest
  ProposalDecision; Proposal has no status attribute.
  A new decision is allowed when there is no decision,
  or the latest outcome is returned or held.
end note

note bottom of ProposalController
  Proposal.recordDecision returns "recorded" or
  "refused" (already decided), as shown in the UC2
  interaction diagrams. No boolean or DecisionResult
  type is added. Save only when the result is "recorded".
end note

note right of DecisionOutcome
  The editor's four decision choices (BR2).
  This is separate from the "recorded" or "refused"
  result of attempting to record a decision.
end note
@enduml
